      "writtenOn": "2023-03-07T18:32:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit (should be done but can be done later):\n\nI prefer to reset emulator state using the `ZTEST_RULE` macro. See https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/emul/emul_smart_battery.c;l\u003d915 for an example of how this is used.\n\nThis way of resetting the emulator provides a bit more abstraction of the emulator to the test. It\u0027s also pretty nice for when someone is writing an integration test and doesn\u0027t necessarily want to special case which emulated device they\u0027re using.\n\nIt also makes the eventual upstreaming of the test easier.",
